WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.707 --> 00:00:03.372
- Me and Pete just hanging out.

00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:04.442
Look at that face.

00:00:04.442 --> 00:00:07.025
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.475
Hi, I'm Liam Payne and
I'm here at Buzzfeed

00:00:14.475 --> 00:00:17.808
and I am about to meet a lot of puppies.

00:00:19.435 --> 00:00:20.435
Look at you!

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:22.530
Hello!

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.809
Oh, you're lovely, aren't you?

00:00:23.809 --> 00:00:25.550
Hello, come here you.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.879
You're a rascal.

00:00:26.879 --> 00:00:28.371
You're gonna be the rascal of the group

00:00:28.371 --> 00:00:29.357
and you also want to join in.

00:00:29.357 --> 00:00:30.391
(laughing)

00:00:30.391 --> 00:00:33.034
This one really likes me.

00:00:33.034 --> 00:00:34.730
I've got an attachment here.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:38.063
All right then, let's do some questions.

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:49.203
I think I would
collaborate best with Zayne

00:00:49.203 --> 00:00:52.382
because we do really
similar type of music.

00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:55.223
And I would say that I
would like our music videos

00:00:55.223 --> 00:00:56.912
to be right here with these puppies

00:00:56.912 --> 00:01:00.579
because this is just
too much fun right now.

00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:05.890
There's talk of maybe
doing a collaboration.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.731
Maybe I'm gonna collaborate
with this guy right here.

00:01:08.731 --> 00:01:10.092
But I can't tell you who it is yet

00:01:10.092 --> 00:01:11.842
but she is an artist.

00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:17.941
It's very open, isn't it?

00:01:17.941 --> 00:01:19.052
Love the question bowl.

00:01:19.052 --> 00:01:21.719
Do you wanna pick me a question?

00:01:25.733 --> 00:01:29.675
What a question to follow
up with that question!

00:01:29.675 --> 00:01:33.842
I would collaborate with Nicky
Minaj I think would be best.

00:01:41.989 --> 00:01:43.932
My favorite part about
touring with the boys

00:01:43.932 --> 00:01:45.752
was when we were younger, we used to spend

00:01:45.752 --> 00:01:47.738
a lot of time together on the tour bus.

00:01:47.738 --> 00:01:49.065
And when we did that first American tour,

00:01:49.065 --> 00:01:50.680
we had a really tiny small bus

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.158
and it was just a lot of
fun and just hanging out

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:54.815
and it was like, I don't know.

00:01:54.815 --> 00:01:56.159
That was the time when we got to

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:00.242
know each other best I
think throughout the band.

00:02:01.771 --> 00:02:02.765
No, I'm not at all.

00:02:02.765 --> 00:02:04.679
I think honestly he's really
really suited for the job

00:02:04.679 --> 00:02:06.671
and I know that Harry's
really good at what he does.

00:02:06.671 --> 00:02:08.073
And I wanted to congratulate the man.

00:02:08.073 --> 00:02:09.807
It's a massive moment, like
being in a Christopher Nolan

00:02:09.807 --> 00:02:11.330
action film, like how amazing, super cool.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.604
I haven't seen it yet but
I am planning on having

00:02:14.604 --> 00:02:17.646
a little event with my
team and some of my family

00:02:17.646 --> 00:02:19.675
and going down and all of
us watching it together

00:02:19.675 --> 00:02:21.895
'cause I wanna make sure
that it's in a night setting.

00:02:21.895 --> 00:02:23.551
I wanna go, I haven't
been to the cinema in ages

00:02:23.551 --> 00:02:25.380
and I'd like to go to the cinema.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.297
You haven't said hello
very much, hello, hello!

00:02:32.512 --> 00:02:37.496
The last text message I sent
was "Check the vids aha"

00:02:37.496 --> 00:02:38.950
to one of my friends 'cause I was doing

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.533
some silly videos on Instagram.

00:02:42.381 --> 00:02:43.636
That was long and boring and I thought

00:02:43.636 --> 00:02:45.749
it was gonna be up right and exciting.

00:02:45.749 --> 00:02:47.152
You make sure you just
stay there the whole time.

00:02:47.152 --> 00:02:49.137
You're just quite chill.

00:02:49.137 --> 00:02:50.294
What's your deal, Pete?

00:02:50.294 --> 00:02:52.800
You're the naughty one of the bunch.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.633
Come here, you.

00:02:53.633 --> 00:02:54.466
Come on.

00:03:01.398 --> 00:03:05.969
Yes I think we will reunite
at some point in the future.

00:03:05.969 --> 00:03:07.007
I'm sure, we have to.

00:03:07.007 --> 00:03:08.374
I mean we've got an album that
we haven't even toured yet

00:03:08.374 --> 00:03:12.541
and I wanna write some more
songs as well with the boys.

00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:18.506
The songwriting process
has been a lot different

00:03:18.506 --> 00:03:20.240
'cause you have to look a lot

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.888
inside yourself for inspiration.

00:03:22.888 --> 00:03:24.755
It was different when I
was writing for the boys

00:03:24.755 --> 00:03:28.191
because you have to have
four people to please

00:03:28.191 --> 00:03:29.763
so in a way, it's kinda easier as well

00:03:29.763 --> 00:03:31.947
but it's hard because, it's very very,

00:03:31.947 --> 00:03:34.558
it just relies on you I guess.

00:03:34.558 --> 00:03:36.293
Which is nice and there's
some really personal songs

00:03:36.293 --> 00:03:38.392
that I've done on that
album and there's some

00:03:38.392 --> 00:03:40.755
that I do my other writers
'cause there are obviously

00:03:40.755 --> 00:03:42.205
great writers in the
world and I've got to work

00:03:42.205 --> 00:03:44.569
with some great people like
Farrell and Ryan Teller

00:03:44.569 --> 00:03:47.123
and obviously Zedd at the
moment which has been great

00:03:47.123 --> 00:03:48.859
so I've been really lucky with the people

00:03:48.859 --> 00:03:50.442
I got to work with.

00:03:55.723 --> 00:03:56.767
Yes and no.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.341
There's loads of different
parts to the album

00:03:58.341 --> 00:04:02.155
so I still can't believe
you're sat here all the time.

00:04:02.155 --> 00:04:03.555
You're so tamed.

00:04:03.555 --> 00:04:05.788
Yeah, and there's some ballads,

00:04:05.788 --> 00:04:09.309
there's some hip hop songs,
there's some more dance music.

00:04:09.309 --> 00:04:11.866
So I think there's a really varied mix

00:04:11.866 --> 00:04:13.354
of different things that we have.

00:04:13.354 --> 00:04:14.437
I don't know how I'm ever gonna separate

00:04:14.437 --> 00:04:17.687
from you ever again; look at your eyes.

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:21.859
My go-to karaoke song would be

00:04:21.859 --> 00:04:25.295
♫ I know when that hotline bling

00:04:25.295 --> 00:04:27.533
♫ Hey, that can only mean one thing

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.783
(laughing)

00:04:31.927 --> 00:04:32.922
There's actually a name for this

00:04:32.922 --> 00:04:34.365
and it's a long something or other phobia

00:04:34.365 --> 00:04:36.224
that they call it; I'm not sure.

00:04:36.224 --> 00:04:39.141
But I'm no longer afraid of spoons.

00:04:41.683 --> 00:04:43.183
My favorite songs.

00:04:44.818 --> 00:04:46.068
That was quick.

00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:54.385
I think I'd like to go in and play arenas.

00:04:54.385 --> 00:04:56.623
I love a big stage and
I like running around.

00:04:56.623 --> 00:04:58.749
I actually measured it one
time when we were on stage

00:04:58.749 --> 00:05:00.773
and we used to do like
six kilometers a night

00:05:00.773 --> 00:05:03.370
every times on, so we're
used to running around

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.917
a big stage so I don't know
how I feel going back to small.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:07.320
I do like the smaller venues as well.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.520
It's nice and intimate but I love to do

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.456
really big shows and I
want to put on a great show

00:05:10.456 --> 00:05:14.623
for you guys with loads of
different elements in it so.

00:05:17.572 --> 00:05:19.884
Oh, I never thought about that.

00:05:19.884 --> 00:05:22.906
I would wake up at around nine.

00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:24.435
Go to the gym for a little bit,

00:05:24.435 --> 00:05:26.958
I'd sit and watch, I'd have the new series

00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:29.813
of Peaky Blinders out
now; that'd be a good day.

00:05:29.813 --> 00:05:32.004
I'm having to wait for ages.

00:05:32.004 --> 00:05:35.267
I would have an in and out burger

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:39.351
'cause they are the
best thing known to man.

00:05:39.351 --> 00:05:40.835
And that would be quite the perfect day.

00:05:40.835 --> 00:05:41.824
Oh, you're back again.

00:05:41.824 --> 00:05:42.657
Hello.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.218
My favorite memory was when we first did

00:05:48.218 --> 00:05:49.961
Madison Square Gardens.

00:05:49.961 --> 00:05:52.489
We popped out the floor
and the crowd is just--

00:05:52.489 --> 00:05:53.322
Oh.

00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:56.821
Where are you going?

00:05:56.821 --> 00:05:57.885
We popped out the floor and it was just

00:05:57.885 --> 00:05:59.915
the most amazing feeling
ever knowing that we were

00:05:59.915 --> 00:06:01.403
in Madison Square Gardens and our album,

00:06:01.403 --> 00:06:03.897
we just broke the record
for debuting at number one

00:06:03.897 --> 00:06:05.550
on the American charts so that was

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.048
a real fond memory of mine.

00:06:08.048 --> 00:06:09.373
How are we doing Pete?

00:06:09.373 --> 00:06:10.623
What's hanging?

00:06:13.969 --> 00:06:17.136
I would say having my missus eye on me

00:06:18.473 --> 00:06:20.378
is always a nice thing so I like to know

00:06:20.378 --> 00:06:21.501
that she's always got her eye on me

00:06:21.501 --> 00:06:25.501
and I've always got my
eye on her which is nice.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:28.840
I would say Pete at this moment in time.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.400
He's just fulfilling life for me.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.051
I want to say thank you to
Buzzfeed for having me today

00:06:33.051 --> 00:06:34.372
but I just wanted to let everybody know

00:06:34.372 --> 00:06:36.516
that all these puppies are adoptable

00:06:36.516 --> 00:06:39.769
from the North Shore
Animal League in America

00:06:39.769 --> 00:06:42.534
so please, if you have a good home,

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:46.062
and you want a nice
lovely puppy like Pete,

00:06:46.062 --> 00:06:47.312
go and get him.

00:06:49.104 --> 00:06:50.754
Look at Pete.

00:06:50.754 --> 00:06:52.325
Oh my God.

00:06:52.325 --> 00:06:54.658
Pete man, you're killing me.

